 her  sister rides into a storm and is knocked  off her horse her solo rides have been  something she's done throughout the  season symbolic of her yearning to be  free both from her duty and a society  that dictates who she can and cannot  love it is ironic then that the person  who ends up saving her is the very man  she met while riding back in episode 1.  throughout the season kate and anthony's  love has been hindered by one thing duty  i'm looking for perfection mother and  you should be too this is the duty i  must fulfill for anthony love is the  last thing he's looking for when it  comes to finding a suitable wife love is  the last thing i desire but if my  children are to be of good stock then  their mother must be of impeccable  quality he treats the courting process  as a duty to be performed setting up  interviews and rehearsed questions  without factoring love into the equation  because for him it is part of his  familial duty it is only out of the  greatest love of my family that i aim to  choose a bride with my head and not my  heart anthony is a slave to duty and  this largely stems from what happened to  his father edmund bridgerton anthony had  much love for his father but when his  father died to an unfortunate bee sting  anthony closed off his heart for him it  was better to shield oneself of pain and  choose not to love than to risk it and  feel that sorrow like he did when his  father died but then after your father  died a wall went up inside you as if  love had become some  some weakness fun fact edmund's favorite  flower was a lilac and wouldn't you know  it but in the vast majority of scenes  you'll see kate wearing that color like  here here and here so if anthony is to  overcome his sense of duty and embrace  love he'll need to learn a valuable  lesson from his mother that it is better  to have loved and lost than to have  never loved at all and i would  undoubtedly feel the same pain i felt  all over again if i had to because real  true love is worth it like anthony  kate's duty to her family prevents her  from finding true love specifically to  her sister edwina to whom she has put  all her time and energy into finding a  match kate is not looking for a husband  at all i'm not here to find a husband  for myself only for my sister it isn't  until episode 6 that kate reveals the  true reason why she will not marry after  her biological father died mary and  edwina took her in treating her as their  own and she will not allow herself to  find love until mary and edwina are  taken care of i promised i would not  consider myself until you and mama were  taken care of kate has been vicariously  living through her younger sister  teaching her everything she needs to  know in order to thrive in high society  what this is actually created is  resentment in her sister for treating  her life as if it were her own you have  spent your life trying to give me  everything i lacked  but really you simply gave me everything  you really wanted for yourself as though  my life were not my own if kate is going  to find true love she like anthony must  put aside her familial duty and realize  that she is deserving of love ironically  enough it is the two mothers who give  both anthony and kate that push to  follow their hearts and express their  love to one another at the featherington  ball after eight episodes of pent up  will they won't they anthony proposes to  kate and she says yes because i cannot  imagine my life without you and that is  why i wish to marry you the season then  fast forward six months after the  marriage of kate and anthony and the two  are happily in love and can finally  express their feelings towards one  another in front of everyone and i half  expected the duke to make an appearance  here saying did i miss anything but a  happy ending is not in store for all our  characters at the end of season 1 it was  revealed that penelope featherington was  the salacious gossip queen lady whistle  down who is actually voiced by none  other than julie andrews in retrospect  it makes sense that pen is whistled down  she has access to all the high society  soirees keeps mainly to herself at the  balls where she picks up on all the hot  gossip and doesn't have men swooning  over her 24 7 affording her ample time  to write these columns as eloise  bridgeton penn's best friend states of  whistle down another thing that the only  reason mrdan writes about such things is  because she is not an actor participant  in them a better word here would be  active participant so at the start of  season 2 we've learned that whistle down  has taken a bit of a break but with  cording season just around the corner  she's ready to sharpen her knives or  should i say quills it's funny then that  in the first scene between penn and  eloise this season she is buying quills  but someone very powerful is adamant on  uncovering whistle down's true identity  and that is the queen the power whistle  down commands in high society is only  matched by her at the stroke of a quill  whistle down can destroy lives which is  why if her identity were revealed it  would be ruinous for penelope the queen  devises a plan to find whistle down's  identity and ultimately one of her foot  soldiers finds eloise visiting a local  print shop little does the queen know  that eloise has actually fallen in love  with a print shop employee  theo sharp and that eloise herself was  searching for whistle down's identity so  the queen corners eloise saying she must  work for her and write good things about  her in the columns or else she'll be  destroyed this puts eloise in a  precarious dilemma because she isn't  whistle down in order to save her friend  penelope must do something unthinkable  write something so terrible about eloise  to prove that whistle down isn't her and  that's exactly what she does stating in  the next column that eloise has been  fraternizing with political radicals  unchaperoned no less a handbag  the plan works but eloise is ruined  making it that much more painful when  she discovers that her best friend did  this to her during the featherington  ball eloise notices how penelope has  picked up on certain gossip and she  begins to put two and two together going  so far as to ransack penelope's room and  finding her secret stash of whistle down  money and effects it's a complete  falling out between these two both of  them saying things that will undoubtedly  make it difficult for them to repair  their friendship but if there's one  thing for certain it's that the writers  are putting penelope in a place where  she is utterly alone at the start of  season 3. she's lost her best friend no  man desires her and the only person she  truly cares for colin bridgerton is  overheard saying that he'd never dream  of courting her if this isn't the start  of a villanark i don't know what is at  the end of the episode penelope picks up  her quill stating that whistle down  cannot keep quiet for long with eloise  knowing her identity i'm not exactly  sure how she's going to keep up this  charade but who knows maybe eloise will  have to keep quiet with what penelope  has on her or perhaps eloise's  credibility is already tarnished  regardless expect a more spiteful  whistle down next season from one  featherington to the other we now take a  look at the baroness porsche who after  the death of her husband archibald in  season 1 eagerly awaits the arrival of  the next owner of the estate jack  featherington porsha hides the fact that  her family is on the cusp of bankruptcy  thus she devises a plan to entrap jack  into marrying her daughter so they can  access his vast wealth in the mining  industry that is until she finds out  he's on the verge of bankruptcy too so  what do two desperate people do  obviously work on an even bigger scheme  to fool the wealthy elite of london into  investing in their sham mining company  so they can take all their cash and run  away to america it's actually colin a  potential investor who uncovers this  plot finding out that the gems he's been  selling are a cheap knockoff knowing  they'll be found out porsche ends up  double-crossing jack taking half of the  money and setting him up as the sole  antagonist of this devious plot and this  is all because jack truly does not care  for her or her children remember this is  the guy who wanted to make out with  porsha even though he was engaged to her  daughter and it's clear to me that you  do not care about them at all so i'm  sending you away with your favorite  person yourself not only that she had  mrs varley forge a signature stating  that as soon as one of her daughters has  a son the estate will pass on to them  this actually sets up some juicy drama  for season 3. it may force the  featherington sisters into competition  with one another to see who can pump out  a sun the quickest in order to gain  control of the estate but there are  still a few loose ends when it comes to  the end of the season and the start of  season 3. we know that netflix has  renewed bridgeton for a third and fourth  season and that executive producer chris  van dusen has stated his goal was to  focus on a different bridgerton sibling  in every one could that mean benedict is  our season 3 lead he did drop out of art  school after finding out his brother  paid for his entry so that's all up in  the air but van dusen has stated that  they quote might have to get creative  when riding these upcoming seasons that  to me signals they aren't going with the  obvious next bridgerton sibling benedict  i'm wondering if that will mean we could  get a time jump and possibly see an  older hyacinth or gregory be the focal  point of next season anything seems to  be on the table colin is also a  possibility however i personally see him  as a bit too young to take on the lead  just yet maybe in two seasons from now  bridgeton's aside we also have edwina  who was supposed to be wed to anthony  she's now single and as the queen hinted  at near the end of the season she's  gonna try to hook her up with her nephew  the prince of russia who we saw briefly  in season one if that actually happens  it means kate and anthony would be  brother-in-law to russian royalty which  i think opens a ton of cool new  possibilities i'm really excited to see  where bridgeton goes it looks like every  season will have its own unique feel and  spin to it which will make it exciting  to watch but what did you think of  bridgerton season 2 i want to hear your  thoughts and theories in the comments  below thanks for watching everyone be  sure to like and subscribe it really  helps the channel out and for more bad  takes you can follow me on twitter and  instagram at think story yt until next  time remember  you

